First one

00:01:30.660 --> 00:01:31.220
First one of the year

00:01:31.220 --> 00:01:31.920
Very first one of the year

00:01:32.420 --> 00:01:33.160
You cool with that?

00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:35.080
Season of giving

00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:35.720
Season of giving

00:01:35.720 --> 00:01:36.220
That'll work

00:01:36.220 --> 00:01:36.920
You guys cool with that?

00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:38.540
Cool

00:01:38.540 --> 00:01:39.900
'Cause this video is brought to you by Lenovo,

00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:40.900
and the Phab 2 Pro

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:43.180
So Lenovo reached out to us,

00:01:43.180 --> 00:01:45.120
and asked if we'd be interested in

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:46.720
making a video about their phone

00:01:46.760 --> 00:01:47.560
the Phab 2 Pro

00:01:48.020 --> 00:01:49.400
What Lenovo does not know is that

00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:51.220
a fan actually emailed us two months ago

00:01:51.220 --> 00:01:52.120
about this phone

00:01:52.680 --> 00:01:55.320
saying they were developing a film-making program

00:01:55.320 --> 00:01:56.220
for this phone

00:01:56.220 --> 00:01:57.020
using "Tango"

00:01:57.020 --> 00:01:57.740
Now, what is "Tango"?

00:01:57.740 --> 00:01:59.200
"Tango" is this piece of technology

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:00.300
that Google has been working on

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:03.620
that let's the phone track its position in 3D space

00:02:04.040 --> 00:02:06.360
So this guy made a piece of software

00:02:06.360 --> 00:02:08.020
that using that 3D tracking

00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:09.340
would stabilize your video

00:02:09.340 --> 00:02:11.240
better than anything else out there

00:02:11.240 --> 00:02:13.300
that does artificial video stabilization

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:14.000
So I said: Yes,

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:14.600
Please send us a phone

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:15.960
because I want to check out that program

00:02:15.960 --> 00:02:16.820
and see how it works

00:02:16.820 --> 00:02:17.720
But before I do,

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:19.960
let me show you guys what "Tango" is

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:22.280
I don't think everybody quite gets this whole...

00:02:22.280 --> 00:02:23.900
I've only seen one demo of this so far

00:02:23.900 --> 00:02:24.400
Yeah

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:25.580
And even that was pretty impressive

00:02:25.580 --> 00:02:26.080
*Niko laughs*

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:27.360
So on the back of this phone,

00:02:27.900 --> 00:02:29.980
is a whole sweet of sensors here

00:02:29.980 --> 00:02:31.680
cameras and I think a depth sensor

00:02:31.740 --> 00:02:32.700
and a couple other things

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:34.740
that are constantly scanning the environment

00:02:34.740 --> 00:02:36.760
But it's basically doing real-time motion tracking

00:02:36.760 --> 00:02:37.480
For example,

00:02:37.480 --> 00:02:38.440
You can pull a video

00:02:38.440 --> 00:02:39.840
And have things overlayed

00:02:40.040 --> 00:02:40.920
in your video

00:02:40.920 --> 00:02:42.680
basically real-time visual effects

00:02:42.880 --> 00:02:44.060
Wren, how do you like your pet?

00:02:44.260 --> 00:02:44.760
Dude

00:02:45.260 --> 00:02:45.900
Best pet

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:47.520
Way better than Obbi

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:48.280
*laughter*

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:49.420
Oh he likes it!

00:02:49.800 --> 00:02:50.300
Oh!

00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:52.460
Alright so we loaded up this program called "Holo"

00:02:52.460 --> 00:02:54.940
which will let you take 3D scanned models

00:02:54.940 --> 00:02:57.740
that are actual people or objects in a room

00:02:57.740 --> 00:02:58.860
and place them in the environment

00:02:58.860 --> 00:02:59.360
So this-

00:02:59.360 --> 00:03:00.400
I think this will show off the tracking

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:01.960
better than anything else

00:03:02.620 --> 00:03:03.740
There's a monkey over there

00:03:04.260 --> 00:03:04.760
He's like...

00:03:05.020 --> 00:03:05.780
Fo' getta 'bout it

00:03:06.880 --> 00:03:07.680
*laughter*

00:03:13.320 --> 00:03:13.820
Yeah

00:03:14.080 --> 00:03:15.280
He's really funny

00:03:17.220 --> 00:03:17.780
I bet...

00:03:18.060 --> 00:03:19.340
He's playing you a song, man!

00:03:20.180 --> 00:03:20.980
*laughter*

00:03:23.920 --> 00:03:24.480
Alright

00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:26.240
Oh my god!

00:03:26.240 --> 00:03:27.820
*laughter*

00:03:27.820 --> 00:03:28.320
That actually-

00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:30.060
It works really- pretty good actually

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:30.800
I'm really suprised

00:03:31.740 --> 00:03:33.520
Ah he's getting taller! He's growing!

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:34.640
He's growing!

00:03:35.340 --> 00:03:36.700
He's like Hodor now!

00:03:37.160 --> 00:03:37.660
*Wren laughing*

00:03:37.660 --> 00:03:38.700
There he is, just chillin'

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:39.200
This guy,

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:40.420
This guy, right here

00:03:40.420 --> 00:03:41.380
Has been with,

00:03:42.120 --> 00:03:43.160
With me on every occasion

00:03:45.300 --> 00:03:46.660
He's not good around guests

00:03:46.660 --> 00:03:47.160
Dang!

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:48.540
The tracking is so good!

00:03:49.320 --> 00:03:50.440
*Niko laughing*

00:03:51.160 --> 00:03:51.660
Wow

00:03:51.920 --> 00:03:52.640
*continues laughing*

00:03:52.640 --> 00:03:53.620
My arms like, wha?

00:03:53.620 --> 00:03:54.700
3 feet behind the zombie

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:56.960
Dang, that is pretty impressive though

00:03:57.600 --> 00:03:58.620
So that's enough messing around

00:03:58.620 --> 00:04:01.100
Hopefully you guys get the idea of how Tango works

00:04:01.220 --> 00:04:02.080
It gives you this-

00:04:06.380 --> 00:04:07.720
Whenever we do visual effects shots,

00:04:07.720 --> 00:04:09.720
we need to put a fake element into a real shot

00:04:13.740 --> 00:04:14.500
Enough games,

00:04:14.500 --> 00:04:16.180
let's go apply this to some film-making

00:04:16.180 --> 00:04:18.720
let's go test out that stabilization program

00:04:21.300 --> 00:04:22.260
He's dancin'!

00:04:22.260 --> 00:04:22.980
Scoot back!

00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:25.340
So I fired up the app,

00:04:25.340 --> 00:04:26.140
it's call "Cinamatic"

00:04:26.140 --> 00:04:27.820
You can check it out on the Google Playstore

00:04:27.820 --> 00:04:29.680
if you happen to have a "Tango" enabled device

00:04:29.680 --> 00:04:30.580
like the Phab 2 Pro

00:04:30.580 --> 00:04:32.760
It actually does the stabilization real-time

00:04:32.760 --> 00:04:34.200
So now I'm recording in real-time,

00:04:34.200 --> 00:04:35.520
it shows me the stablization

00:04:35.520 --> 00:04:36.940
This is much more stable than any sort of like

00:04:36.940 --> 00:04:38.860
"Gyroscope"-based stabilizer

00:04:38.860 --> 00:04:40.260
like you get with "Hyperlapse"

00:04:40.260 --> 00:04:42.040
'Cause it's getting an actual 3D track

00:04:42.040 --> 00:04:43.060
of the environment

00:04:43.060 --> 00:04:44.600
It's stabilizing off of that

00:04:44.600 --> 00:04:45.860
So it's rock solid

00:04:45.860 --> 00:04:46.800
it's like a steady cam'

00:04:47.080 --> 00:04:47.720
It's pretty great

00:04:48.340 --> 00:04:49.660
Sprint as fast as you can!

00:04:57.360 --> 00:04:58.480
Dude, that's like a steady cam'

00:04:58.700 --> 00:05:00.220
